  "term": "pseudobulbar affect",
  "definition": "Pseudobulbar affect is a condition involving sudden, uncontrollable episodes of laughing or crying that do not fit the situation. It can occur after certain neurological illnesses or injuries that disrupt the brain’s control of emotional expression.",
